        "text_YYjgFV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Neil Doniger, as Vice President of NADCO Tapes and Labels, brings a deep-rooted legacy to the company, being a third-generation tape and label manufacturer. His family history spans across the distribution and converting industries, with his grandfather in distribution and his father in converting. This long-standing heritage paved the way for Neil’s vision, which took shape in 1988 when he expanded the business by introducing printing and die cutting, opening a shop in Connecticut.</p><p>Shortly after, Neil met and married Rena, who became the company’s accountant, adding a personal and collaborative aspect to the growing enterprise. In 1993, the couple moved the business to New Hampshire, and NADCO continued to grow its unique offering—providing both printing and die cutting, as well as converting. This combination of services remains one of the distinguishing factors of the company, setting it apart in an industry that often specializes in just one aspect of the label-making process.</p><p>With 37 years in the industry, NADCO has stood the test of time, and much of its continued success can be attributed to Neil’s commitment to personalized service and innovation. Unlike many businesses, where a sale might be passed through a chain of contacts, every sale at NADCO goes through Neil himself. He enjoys the process of helping clients bring their visions to life, whether they are small businesses, large corporations, or even clients in industries like Tesla, where Neil has engaged in R&D work.</p>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "badge_rTMetq",
        "heading_brVgWK",
